'''Weak & Mildly Acidic''' (脆弱性と弱酸性 ''Seijakusei to Jakusan-sei'', '''Weakness and Mild Acidity''') is the 28th sub-chapter of [[Stories of Legend]]. It was added in [[Version 5.0 Update|Version 5.0]] and is available up to {{4c}} difficulty.

==Difficulty==
Just like [[Body & Soul]], this sub-chapter has a mix of easy and difficult stages. Expect to see a large variety of enemies. Also, two new enemies will appear - [[Two Can]] and the semi-unique [[Codename "Red Riding"]]. Two Can can create highly damaging [[Wave Attack]]s, while Codename "Red Riding" has exceptional health and long range. In terms of difficulty, the hardest stages are probably [[At Least I'm a Cat]], which spams several enemies of several traits, and [[Learned to Love]], the first SoL stage to be based around rushing down a [[:Category:Long Distance Enemies|Long Distance enemy]].
{{LegendDiff|120|140|100}}

==New Features==
This sub-chapter introduces two new enemies:
*[[Two Can]]: A [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]]/[[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] enemy with high attack damage and a 100% chance to perform Lv.2 [[Wave Attack]]. However, his health isn't too high compared to similar enemies.
*[[Codename "Red Riding"]]: A [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemy with massive health and very high attack damage, along with insanely long range. Her range is so long that she can hit the [[Cat Base]] if she advances just 1/5th of the battlefield. Beware!
*While not his first appearance in-game, [[CyberFace]] makes his first appearance in the Stories of Legend here. He is a [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemy with massive attack power and Wave Attacks, but low enough health to die from any [[Critical Hit]].
When [[Learned to Love]] is completed, players have a 30% chance to unlock [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Red Riding Mina]] (guaranteed if a [[Treasure Radar]] is used).

